From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d: Clamp wave size for Silent Hill: Townfall.

Some of its compute shaders require WaveSize 32. On wave64-only GPUs
such as Vega and Renoir, vkd3d-proton rejects them ("Required WaveSize
range [32, 32], but supported range is [64, 64].") and the game hangs
the GPU with VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST when entering Sta. Amelia.

Applying CLAMP_WAVE_SIZE_TO_THREAD_GROUP32 to all shaders, as for other
UE5 games, let the reporter get past that point on RADV Renoir.

Co-authored-by: Gilberto Ferreira <10462980+gilbertoferreira@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libs/vkd3d/vkd3d_proton_app_workarounds.json | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/libs/vkd3d/vkd3d_proton_app_workarounds.json
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/vkd3d_proton_app_workarounds.json
@@ -707,6 +707,14 @@
         "perEntryQuirks" : {},
         "perHashQuirks" : {}
       },
+      "name" : "Townfall.exe"
+    },
+    {
+      "shaderQuirks" : {
+        "defaultQuirks" : [ "CLAMP_WAVE_SIZE_TO_THREAD_GROUP32" ],
+        "perEntryQuirks" : {},
+        "perHashQuirks" : {}
+      },
       "comparator" : "STARTS_WITH",
       "name" : "PioneerGame"
     },
